    <briefdescription>
<para>Matrix-form encoding of a <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monomial_ordering" kindref="compound">MonomialOrdering</ref></computeroutput> used by the Groebner walk algorithm. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Every monomial ordering can be expressed as a matrix <computeroutput>M</computeroutput> so <computeroutput>m_1 &lt; m_2</computeroutput> iff the first non-zero entry of <computeroutput>M (exp(m_2) - exp(m_1))</computeroutput> is positive. This class extracts that matrix from a <computeroutput>MonomialOrdering*</computeroutput> and stores each row in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_order_matrix_a2d0e58e847f17e95a02b2aad866c6bec_1a2d0e58e847f17e95a02b2aad866c6bec" kindref="member">order</ref>[i]</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>value(i, m)</computeroutput> is the inner product <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_order_matrix_a2d0e58e847f17e95a02b2aad866c6bec_1a2d0e58e847f17e95a02b2aad866c6bec" kindref="member">order</ref>[i] . exp(m)</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>compare(m1, m2)</computeroutput> walks the rows until one differs, and <computeroutput>minpart(m)</computeroutput> returns the first row that takes a non-zero value on <computeroutput>m</computeroutput>. Used internally by <computeroutput><ref refid="gb-walk_8cpp" kindref="compound">gb-walk.cpp</ref></computeroutput> to interpolate between monomial orderings during a GB walk. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
